# Dev Notes 45 — Runtime Memory Module Blueprint Reconciliation v1

**Date:** 2026-06-17  
**Branch:** `runtime-memory-module-blueprint-reconciliation-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to main and main-inspected for the declared docs-only blueprint-reconciliation scope.

---

## 1. Purpose

This docs-only branch reconciles the planned Runtime Memory Module into the existing Runtime System Blueprint v1.

The branch makes the memory/state direction explicit while preserving the existing architecture boundary:

```text
Runtime Dev remains the execution substrate.
The Runtime Memory Module is a Runtime Dev substrate module.
The Cognitive Graph Runtime remains a future control-layer track.
Runtime Dev stays graph-compatible without becoming graph-dependent.
```

This is design documentation only. It does not implement memory storage, SQLite, PostgreSQL, Qdrant, JanusGraph, retrieval, promotion, checkpointing, context packing, graph/control behavior, capability execution, backend adapters, public APIs, runtime wiring, worker behavior, or tests.

